        "text": "100"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "108"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Prime factorisation",
        "body": "$2016=2^5\\cdot3^2\\cdot7$. For a perfect square every prime must have an even exponent, so the multiplier must supply (at least) one more $2$ and one $7$: $2\\cdot7=14$ works, giving $2^6\\cdot3^2\\cdot7^2=(8\\cdot3\\cdot7)^2=168^2$. None of the other options contains the factor $7$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 14**"
      }
    ],
