    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "In the diagram $\\triangle STR$ and $\\triangle YTR$ are isosceles triangles with $ST=SR$ and $YT=YR$. If $\\angle YTR=36^\\circ$ and $\\angle SRY=24^\\circ$, then $\\angle TSR$ is equal to",
    "image": "qimages/samf/senior-2016-r1/q05.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$50^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$60^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$70^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$40^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$30^\\circ$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Chase angles",
        "body": "$YT=YR$ gives $\\angle YRT=\\angle YTR=36^\\circ$. So $\\angle SRT=24^\\circ+36^\\circ=60^\\circ$. $ST=SR$ gives $\\angle STR=\\angle SRT=60^\\circ$, so $\\angle TSR=180^\\circ-60^\\circ-60^\\circ=60^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $60^\\circ$**"
      }
    ],
