    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "In rugby it is possible to score 3, 5 or 7 points at a time. If South Africa wins the next Rugby World Cup and scores 34 points in the final, the highest number of times 3 points could have been scored by South Africa is",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "6"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "7"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "8"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "9"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "10"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Try the largest counts",
        "body": "Write $34=3a+5b+7c$ and maximise $a$. $a=10$ leaves $4$, which cannot be made from $5$s and $7$s. $a=11$ leaves $1$, impossible. Larger $a$ exceeds $34$. $a=9$ leaves $7=7\\cdot1$: $9\\times3+7=34$ works.\n\n**Answer: (D) 9**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "number-theory",
      "arithmetic"
    ],
