    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "In $\\triangle RUG$, $RU=10$ cm, $UG=21$ cm, $RG=17$ cm and $RY$ is perpendicular to $UG$ at point $Y$. The length of $RY$, in cm, is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/senior-2016-r1/q14.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "8"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "7"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "6"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "8.1"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Pythagoras twice",
        "body": "Let $UY=x$, so $YG=21-x$ and $RY^2=100-x^2=289-(21-x)^2$. Expanding: $100-x^2=289-441+42x-x^2$, so $42x=252$, $x=6$ and $RY=\\sqrt{100-36}=8$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 8**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Heron's formula",
        "body": "Sides $10,17,21$: $s=24$, area $=\\sqrt{24\\cdot14\\cdot7\\cdot3}=\\sqrt{7056}=84$. Then $RY=\\dfrac{2\\cdot84}{21}=8$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 8**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
  },
