    "prompt": "A sequence of 2 016 terms is constructed as follows: The first two terms of the sequence are both equal to 3. Starting from the third term, each subsequent term is the sum of the preceding two terms. Each of the terms of this sequence $3,3,6,9,\\ldots$ is now divided by 2 and the remainders are added. What is the sum of all the remainders of the 2016 terms?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "504"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "1 008"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "1 344"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "1 512"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "2 016"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Parity pattern",
        "body": "Parities: odd, odd, then odd+odd=even, odd+even=odd, even+odd=odd, odd+odd=even, ... The pattern odd, odd, even repeats every $3$ terms. Each cycle contributes remainders $1+1+0=2$. There are $2016/3=672$ cycles, so the sum is $672\\times2=1344$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 1 344**"
      }
    ],
