    "points": 5,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "$A$ and $B$ are opposite vertices of a regular hexagon. $C$ and $D$ are midpoints of two opposite sides. If the area of the hexagon is 126, then $AB\\times CD$ is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/senior-2016-r1/q18.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "129"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "132"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$84\\sqrt3$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "168"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "248"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Use the side length",
        "body": "Let the side be $s$. Then $AB=2s$ and $CD=s\\sqrt3$ (twice the apothem $\\frac{\\sqrt3}2s$), so $AB\\times CD=2\\sqrt3\\,s^2$. The area of the hexagon is $\\frac{3\\sqrt3}2s^2=126$, so $\\sqrt3\\,s^2=84$ and $AB\\times CD=168$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 168**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Compare areas",
        "body": "Cut the hexagon into $6$ congruent equilateral triangles. The rectangle with sides $AB$ and $CD$ around the hexagon also contains four right triangles which fit together into $2$ more such equilateral triangles. So its area is $\\frac86\\times126=168$, and this equals $AB\\times CD$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 168**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry"
    ],
    "difficulty": 3,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
